sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Gateway as MaaS Gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant PreProc as payload-pre-processing<br/>9004/TCP gRPC
    participant Authorino as Kuadrant Authorino<br/>WasmPlugin
    participant MaaSAPI as maas-api<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant PostProc as payload-processing<br/>9004/TCP gRPC
    participant KServe as KServe Model<br/>80/443 TCP
    participant ExtProvider as External Provider<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant PostgreSQL as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP

    Note over Client,PostgreSQL: Flow 1: User Token Model Inference

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/models/model:predict<br/>Auth: Bearer Token (OpenShift)
    Gateway->>PreProc: ext_proc (pre-auth)<br/>Extract model name → X-Gateway-Model-Name
    PreProc-->>Gateway: Request headers modified
    Gateway->>Authorino: AuthPolicy evaluation<br/>kubernetesTokenReview
    Authorino->>MaaSAPI: POST /internal/v1/api-keys/validate<br/>(NetworkPolicy protected)
    MaaSAPI-->>Authorino: Validation result
    Authorino-->>Gateway: Auth decision + metadata
    Gateway->>PostProc: ext_proc (post-auth)<br/>API translation, header guard
    PostProc-->>Gateway: Request transformed
    Gateway->>KServe: Forward to LLMInferenceService<br/>mTLS (mesh)
    KServe-->>Gateway: Inference Response
    Gateway-->>Client: JSON Response

    Note over Client,PostgreSQL: Flow 2: API Key Model Inference

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/models/model:predict<br/>Auth: Bearer sk-oai-*
    Gateway->>PreProc: ext_proc (pre-auth)<br/>Model name extraction + provider resolution
    PreProc-->>Gateway: Headers set
    Gateway->>Authorino: Plain credential extraction<br/>(api-keys auth)
    Authorino->>MaaSAPI: POST /internal/v1/api-keys/validate<br/>SHA-256 hash lookup
    MaaSAPI->>PostgreSQL: Query API key hash<br/>TLS (optional)
    PostgreSQL-->>MaaSAPI: Key metadata + permissions
    MaaSAPI-->>Authorino: Key valid + user identity
    Authorino->>MaaSAPI: POST /internal/v1/subscriptions/select<br/>Select subscription for rate limiting
    MaaSAPI-->>Authorino: Selected subscription
    Authorino-->>Gateway: Auth OK + rate limit metadata
    Gateway->>PostProc: ext_proc (post-auth)<br/>Credential injection from Secret
    PostProc-->>Gateway: Credentials injected
    Gateway->>KServe: Forward with injected creds
    KServe-->>Gateway: Inference Response
    Gateway-->>Client: JSON Response

    Note over Client,PostgreSQL: Flow 3: External Model Routing

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/models/ext-model:predict<br/>Auth: Bearer Token or API Key
    Gateway->>PreProc: ext_proc (pre-auth)<br/>Resolve external provider
    PreProc-->>Gateway: Provider resolved
    Gateway->>Authorino: AuthPolicy evaluation
    Authorino-->>Gateway: Auth OK
    Gateway->>PostProc: ext_proc (post-auth)<br/>API translation + credential injection<br/>(from ExternalModel credentialRef Secret)
    PostProc-->>Gateway: Request transformed with provider API key
    Gateway->>ExtProvider: HTTPS/443<br/>TLS 1.2+<br/>API Key (injected)
    ExtProvider-->>Gateway: Provider Response
    Gateway-->>Client: Translated Response

    Note over Client,PostgreSQL: Flow 4: API Key Lifecycle

    Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/api-keys<br/>Auth: Bearer Token (Authorino)
    Gateway->>MaaSAPI: Create API Key request<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    MaaSAPI->>PostgreSQL: Store key hash (SHA-256)<br/>5432/TCP
    PostgreSQL-->>MaaSAPI: Key stored
    MaaSAPI-->>Gateway: API Key (sk-oai-* format)
    Gateway-->>Client: API Key response

    Note over MaaSAPI,PostgreSQL: CronJob: Expired key cleanup
    MaaSAPI->>PostgreSQL: DELETE expired ephemeral keys<br/>(scheduled via CronJob)
